invariant: INV-17
file: src/aead_avx512.c
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: aead_avx512_seal returns without calling avx512_wipe_registers, so the
  key, the keystream, the powers of r and the lanes' sums stay in the
  512-bit registers after the call. Every tag is still right. The script
  compiles the file for x86-64 and requires the call in the seal.

--- old
    // the vector registers, and the compiler clears none of them on return.
    lanes_wipe_registers();
--- new
    // the vector registers, and the compiler clears none of them on return.
